    "result_text": "The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) computed at creation.\n\n**New computation, in one place** \u2014 `util/MembershipLevel.java`:\n- Starts at `1`, `+1` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at `3` (4 reserved for tenure). A pure function of the owner's own fields, mirroring the existing `CityRegion` utility style \u2014 so both the response mapper and the audit line reuse it instead of duplicating the rule.\n\n**Changes wired to it:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 swapped the `membershipTier` string/enum property for `membershipLevel` (`integer`, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`), which regenerates `OwnerDto`. This removes `membershipTier` from the response in favour of `membershipLevel`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 the `@Mapping` target is now `membershipLevel`, and the old `membershipTier(...)` method (with its GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE + household logic) is replaced by a one-line `membershipLevel(...)` delegating to the utility.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (the thing that formerly would carry tier), using the same utility.\n- `CountHousehold.java` \u2014 dropped the now-stale javadoc `@link` to the deleted `membershipTier` method.\n\nNote: household size no longer feeds membership (the new rule uses only email + namesake uniqueness), matching the spec; the `householdSize` field/step is untouched as it's out of scope.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (unique name + email \u2192 level 3) passes, and the full build is green. The audit output confirms it end-to-end: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`.",
